-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/80a685a2-a3b3-4dd5-ade8-cbdbe9c46db7
-- title:
--   $g$ is a version of the conditional risk $x\mapsto\mathbb E[f(X,Y)\mid X=x]$
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a law of $(X,Y)$ on $\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R$ and $f$ a function of $(X,Y)$. A function $g:\mathbb R^d\to\mathbb R$ is a **version of the conditional risk** of $f$ when
--
--   $$
--   g(X)=\mathbb E[f(X,Y)\mid X]\qquad P\text{-almost surely}.
--   $$
--
--   Assumption A3 asks for a version of $x\mapsto\mathbb E[\ell(\theta;(x,Y))\mid X=x]$ that is Lipschitz; this predicate lets a theorem take that version as data.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The conditional expectation is Mathlib's `condExp` with respect to the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the first coordinate. It is $0$ when $f$ is not integrable, so each theorem supplies integrability, directly or through A1 and A3.
-- source:
--   Duchi, Hashimoto & Namkoong, Distributionally Robust Losses for Latent Covariate Mixtures, arXiv:2007.13982v2, §1, p.2, and Assumption A3, p.9

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory

namespace LatentMixDRO

/-- `g` is a version of the conditional risk `x ↦ E[f(X, Y) | X = x]` of `f` under `P`:
`g(X)` agrees `P`-almost surely with the conditional expectation of `f` given the `σ`-algebra
generated by the first coordinate.

Duchi, Hashimoto & Namkoong, arXiv:2007.13982v2, §1, p.2 (display (1)) and Assumption A3, p.9.

**Formalization Note.** The paper's Lipschitz assumption on `x ↦ E[ℓ(θ; (x, Y)) | X = x]` refers to
a version of the conditional expectation; this predicate lets a theorem take that version as
data. Mathlib's `condExp` is `0` for a non-integrable `f`, so a theorem using this predicate must
supply integrability of `f` (directly, or through boundedness and the Lipschitz property, which
make `f` almost everywhere equal to a continuous bounded function). -/
def IsCondRisk {d : ℕ} (P : Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) × ℝ))
    (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) × ℝ → ℝ) (g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (g ∘ Prod.fst) =ᵐ[P] P[f | MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.fst inferInstance]

end LatentMixDRO


